From: CEB-GNRD maintainers <bmc@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ncsi: retry discovery after an empty initial probe

A host-powered controller can fail to answer the first NC-SI enumeration.
The probe still marks the device PROBED; subsequent interface starts then
return ENODEV from channel selection without issuing discovery commands.

On the next start, clear PROBED only when there are no discovered channels.
Reuse the existing probe state machine and request timeout handling. Keep
known channels, package/channel selection policy and external link failure
handling unchanged. The board userspace monitor bounds restart frequency.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/net/ncsi/ncsi-manage.c
+++ b/net/ncsi/ncsi-manage.c
@@ -1817,10 +1817,36 @@
 int ncsi_start_dev(struct ncsi_dev *nd)
 {
 	struct ncsi_dev_priv *ndp = TO_NCSI_DEV_PRIV(nd);
+	struct ncsi_package *np;
+	struct ncsi_channel *nc;
+	bool has_channel = false;
 
 	if (nd->state != ncsi_dev_state_registered &&
 	    nd->state != ncsi_dev_state_functional)
 		return -ENOTTY;
+
+	/* A host-powered NIC can be absent during the first enumeration.
+	 * Finishing that pass sets PROBED even when no channel answered.
+	 * Starting the interface again must retry discovery in that case,
+	 * rather than forever trying to configure an empty channel list.
+	 * Preserve existing channels and user selection policy; lack of
+	 * external carrier alone is not a reason to discard discovery.
+	 */
+	if (ndp->flags & NCSI_DEV_PROBED) {
+		NCSI_FOR_EACH_PACKAGE(ndp, np) {
+			NCSI_FOR_EACH_CHANNEL(np, nc) {
+				has_channel = true;
+				break;
+			}
+			if (has_channel)
+				break;
+		}
+		if (!has_channel) {
+			ndp->flags &= ~(NCSI_DEV_PROBED | NCSI_DEV_HWA);
+			netdev_info(nd->dev,
+				    "NCSI: No discovered channels, retrying probe\n");
+		}
+	}
 
 	if (!(ndp->flags & NCSI_DEV_PROBED)) {
 		ndp->package_probe_id = 0;
